{"study_accession":"PRJNA1330472","secondary_study_accession":"SRP621533","title":"Case Report: A retrotransposon insertion in the ATP7A gene results in premature stop codons and causes Menkes diseas","description":"Pathogenic variants in the ATP7A gene, which encodes a transmembrane copper transporter P-type ATPase, cause a rare X-linked recessive disorder of copper metabolism, known as Menkes disease. Here we describe a 3-year-old boy with progressive neurodegeneration, intractable epilepsy, connective tissue disturbances, and peculiar kinky hair. A retrotransposon insertion (~500 bp) in exon 3 of the ATP7A gene was discovered by WES and sequence analysis. The insertion bears hallmarks of target-primed reverse transcription. Using PCR and RNA-seq, we documented the dramatic decrease in ATP7A transcript production in the patient. This observation highlights the importance of identifying retrotransposon disease genes for diagnosis.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":3,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN51523151","study_accession":"PRJNA1330472","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"RNAseq sample","description":"RNAseq sample","sex":"male","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2025-09-21","attributes":[["isolate","huanzhe"],["age","6 months"],["biomaterial_provider","Mengyao Kou"],["collection_date","2020-05-20"],["geo_loc_name","China:Heilongjiang"],["sex","male"],["tissue","peripheral blood"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR35491206","experiment_accession":"SRX30567681","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":47020892,"base_count":14106267600,"first_public":"2025-09-21","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: huanzhe RNAseq"}],"labels":[]},{"sample_accession":"SAMN51523152","study_accession":"PRJNA1330472","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"RNAseq sample","description":"RNAseq sample","sex":"male","geo_